From 9b68f702d5667395fd7dda890238414b8c5f5f82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cylewitruk <cyle.witruk@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:22:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep an open connection's keys and the session's OT state out
 of unasked use

Proofs about a connection which is still open no longer disclose a
traffic key because everything in one direction happens to be revealed:
the key is disclosed only when the prover asks. A connection can be
carried and forwarded without committing to it when it ends, so its end
does not draw on OT state shared with the proofs of other connections.
Commitments to plaintext which is authenticated with a disclosed key but
not revealed are refused.
